# SupTable5_script.py
This is a python script to generate coding count analysis table. It is 
	
## Usage
 
To run SupTable5_script.py, your command should be in the following format (the contents in `[]` are optional):

	python SupTable5_script.py -I <JOB_NAME> [-s SIB_FILE] [-R RAW_FILE_PATH] [-r ROLES_FILE] [-g SAMPLE_INFORMATION] [-m MUTABILITY_FILE][-o OUTPUT_PATH]

### Required arguments
- `-I <job_name>`: replace `<job_name>` with a name you preferred for the current job. The output files will be stored in folder with this name.

### Optional arguments
  -s SIB_FILE, --sib_file SIB_FILE
                        Path to sibling information file. Used to exclude siblings with ASD risk. Default path is: "/fs/cbsuhy01/storage/NetFlow_ASD/Week8_429/individuals_registration.csv"
  -R RAW_FILE_PATH, --raw_file_path RAW_FILE_PATH
                        Path to UCSF raw mutation files folder. Default path is: "/fs/cbsuhy01/storage/NetFlow_ASD/Week8_429/UCSF_raw/"
  -r ROLES_FILE, --roles_file ROLES_FILE
                        Path to roles file. Used to exclude multiplex family, and siblings with ASD risk.
  -g SAMPLE_INFORMATION, --sample_information SAMPLE_INFORMATION
                        Path to sample information file. Contains the information of sex, phenotype (whether case or sib). The default path is "/fs/cbsuhy01/storage/NetFlow_ASD/Week8/SSC+SPARK+KOR-STAR_parsed.txt".
  -m MUTABILITY_FILE, --Mutability_file MUTABILITY_FILE
                        Path to Mutability file.
  -o OUTPUT_PATH, --output_path OUTPUT_PATH
                        [OPTIONAL] Path to the job folder. If not specified, the job folder will be stored in the default output folder
  -I JOB_NAME, --job_name JOB_NAME
                        Please specify a name for your job. The output files will be stored with this name
Here is an example of your command:

	python SupTable5_script.py -I test_script
	
If you run the above command, the output should be found in your specified output_path + /job_name/ or (./Test_Output + /job_name/ by default), including the following 4 folders: `/DNV/`, `/Transmitted/`, `/Untransmitted/`, `/Summary/`. To get an idea of what the output files should look like, please see example output files in `/fs/cbsuhy01/storage/NetFlow_ASD/Week8/Final_ASD_github/test_902`.
The main output file (coding count table) will be stored in the path "./Summary/Total_CodingAnalysis_Table.txt"

## Output files
- `{job_name}/{Summary}/`
	This is a folder containing the summary files. There are three files in this folder. Two of them are the count tables for DNV and Transmitted variants, respectively. The overall coding count table is the following:

Total_CodingAnalysis_Table.txt

	This a tab-separated file containing the count information for each coding variant type. The first line is a header. Twenty one columns are present:
  1. gene	(gene name)
  2. gene_gencodeV33	(gene name in gencodeV33 annotation)
  3. gene_id	(ENSEMBL gene id)
  4. chromosome	(chromsome of gene)
  5. pLI	(probability of being loss-of-function intolerant constraint metric)
  6. LOEUF	(loss-of-function observed/expected upper bound fraction constraint metric)
  7. mut.ptv	(De Novo protein truncating (lof) mutation rate)
  8. mut.misb	(De Novo Missense B (misB; MPC > = 2) mutation rate)
  9. mut.misa	(De Novo Missense A (misA; 1 <= MPC < 2) mutation rate)
  10. DNV.ptv	(Number of De Novo PTVs in affected offspring)
  11. DNV.ptv.sib	(Number of De Novo PTVs in unaffected offspring)
  12. DNV.misb	(Number of De Novo misBs in affected offspring)
  13. DNV.misb.sib	(Number of De Novo misBs in unaffected offspring)
  14. DNV.misa	(Number of De Novo misAs in affected offspring)
  15. DNV.misa.sib	(Number of De Novo misAs in unaffected offspring)
  16. Transmitted.ptv	(Number of transmitted PTVs to affected offspring)
  17. Transmitted.ptv.sib	(Number of transmitted PTVs to unaffected offspring)
  18. Transmitted.misb	(Number of transmitted misBs to affected offspring)
  19. Transmitted.misb.sib	(Number of transmitted misBs to unaffected offspring)
  20. Transmitted.misa	(Number of transmitted misAs to affected offspring)
  21. Transmitted.misa.sib	(Number of transmitted misAs to unaffected offspring)

- `{job_name}/{DNV}/`
	This is a folder containing all the intermediate files produced for De Novo variant analysis.

- `{job_name}/{Transmitted}/`
	This is a folder containing all the intermediate files produced for Transmitted variant analysis.

- `{job_name}/{Untransmitted}/`
	This is a folder containing all the intermediate files produced for Untransmitted variant analysis.
